    <h1>RLHF: Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback</h1>
    <p>Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback (RLHF) is a technique used to fine-tune language models based on human preferences, ensuring their output is more helpful, honest, and harmless (often abbreviated as "HHH").</p>
    
    <h2>The RLHF Process</h2>
    <p>Typically, human labelers rank different outputs from a language model, and these rankings are used to train a separate "reward model." This reward model then acts as a score-keeper for the language model during its second phase of training with reinforcement learning.</p>
    
    <h2>Why it Matters</h2>
    <p>RLHF is what makes modern AI assistants like ChatGPT so refined. Without it, models can sometimes provide technically true but unhelpful or even dangerous responses. RLHF helps bridge the gap between simple prediction and human-like interaction.</p>

    <p>Try searching for "HHH" or "Fine-tuning" in the agent!</p>
